# ENT-5 — Queue, Retry & Failed Job Governance (LOCKED)

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/queue-retry-failed-job-governance.md`.
Runbook: `docs/architecture/queue-worker-operations-runbook.md`.
Gate: `php artisan foundation:queue-retry-failed-job-check --strict`.

- Queue, retry, failed job, and worker behavior must follow ENT-5. Any new
  `ShouldQueue` job/listener must define or inherit approved
  timeout/retry/backoff/idempotency behavior and must be covered by the
  governance check.
- New queued jobs extend `App\Support\Queue\EnterpriseQueueJob` (preferred),
  use `App\Support\Queue\EnterpriseQueueRetryDefaults`, or explicitly declare
  `$tries`, `$backoff`/`backoff()`, and `$timeout` within the caps in
  `config/queue_governance.php` → `ent5_retry_failed_job.retry_standards`
  (defaults tries=3, backoff=[10,60,180], timeout=120; caps tries≤5, timeout≤600).
- `sync` queue connection is local/testing only; pilot/staging/production use
  `database` (or `redis` after readiness GO). Failed jobs stay on
  `database-uuids` + `failed_jobs` table — never disabled.
- Allowed queue names: `default`, `reports`, `notifications`, `maintenance`.
- Jobs touching payments, invoices, inventory, lab candidate generation, or
  notifications must be idempotent (QUEUE-1 IdempotencyService); a committed
  payment is never rolled back because a secondary job failed; no job
  auto-sends WhatsApp; no auto LabOrder from RME payment; no PII/KTP/NIK or
  secrets in queue payloads.
- Never automate destructive queue commands (flush/clear/bulk failed-job
  deletion) in app code, schedulers, or deploy scripts — operator-run per the
  runbook only. Deploys never start queue workers.
